    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite passes (1 test, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field derived from an owner's own fields, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\nTwo changes, both following the existing pattern for computed read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field), documented with the format and example `SMI-0007-M26`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that computes it:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   Using `% 100` with `%02d` zero-pads correctly (e.g. year 2026 \u2192 `26`, year 2007 \u2192 `07`), keeping it consistent with the acceptance test which reads `YY` as the two digits at positions 2\u20133 of the ISO date string.\n\nThe field is purely derived from the owner's persisted `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, so it needs no schema/storage changes and is seed-independent, matching the test's expectation.",
